  "live_records": {
    "q-3646": {
      "dom_id": "step-q3646",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{m}{{n}^{2}m+2{n}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{2m+4}{m}?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor all of the expressions and cancel any terms that appear in both a numerator and a denominator. Then, we multiply the numerators and the denominators as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{m}{{n}^{2}m+2{n}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{2m+4}{m} & =\\frac{m}{{n}^{2}(m+2)}\\frac{2(m+2)}{m} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{m}}{{n}^{2}\\cancel{(m+2)}}\\frac{2\\cancel{(m+2)}}{\\cancel{m}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
