      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$\\frac{{m}^{3}}{2n}\\cdot \\frac{4{n}^{2}}{{m}^{2}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We multiply the numerators and the denominators as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{m}^{3}}{2n}\\cdot \\frac{4{n}^{2}}{{m}^{2}} & =\\frac{{m}^{3}\\cdot 4{n}^{2}}{2n\\cdot {m}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{m}^{3}{n}^{2}}{2n{m}^{2}} \\\\  & =2mn\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In the above example, we performed some cancellations after multiplying. However, with more complex expressions, it's often easier to cancel *before* multiplying.",
